#14 8.152 
#14 8.152 The prompter used in this script allows you to use shell variables and
#14 8.152 backticks in your answers.  You may use $1, $2, etc...  to refer to the words
#14 8.152 in the default answer, as if the default line was a set of arguments given to a
#14 8.152 script shell.  This means you may also use $* to repeat the whole default line,
#14 8.152 so you do not have to re-type everything to add something to the default.
#14 8.152 
#14 8.152 Every time there is a substitution, you will have to confirm.  If there is an
#14 8.152 error (e.g. an unmatched backtick), the default answer will remain unchanged
